			"Message": "style(Common): Remove superfluous blank lines between doc comment paragraphs\n\nContinue the crate-wide doc comment normalization by removing the empty `///` separator lines that break the logical flow between a doc comment's opening summary and its following narrative paragraph across 80+ files.\n\nKey modifications:\n- Strip all `///` blank-line separators between the opening sentence (or short paragraph) and the subsequent \"Implemented by\", \"Uses the\", \"Includes the\", \"Defines\", or \"Contains\" continuation in every Service, Effect, DTO, Trait, and module-level doc comment\n- Rewrite module-level `//!` doc comments from the \"This module defines...\" pattern to the stronger, subject-led \"Defines the abstract contract for...\" style aligning with the prior commit's trait-level conventions\n- Clean up a few additional doc comment issues discovered along the way:\n  - `ActionEffect.rs`: Replace the weak \"It is a data structure that...\" second paragraph with a tighter explanation of the closure-based pattern\n  - `IPCProvider.rs`: Shorten \"This method does not wait for a response\" to \"Does not wait for a response\" on the SendNotification doc\n  - `TransportStrategy.rs`: Fix a lowercase \"provides\" that slipped through when its introductory paragraph was rewritten\n  - `DiagnosticManager.rs`: Remove stray blank lines between `# Parameters` bullet items\n  - `IsWorkspaceTrusted.rs`: Remove redundant blank line before the \"Uses the...\" paragraph\n  - `WorkspaceEditApplier.rs`: Remove redundant \"complex\" from \"isolates the logic of applying such edits\"\n\nImpact: Clean, flowing doc comment prose across every service contract in the Common crate, with no orphan blank lines between logically connected paragraphs.",
			"SHA": "284b05c45e6520bf54a70eeb55d0c9b1ec7632d2"
